# Copy to .dev.vars for local development (gitignored).
# Production values are set with `wrangler secret put <NAME>`.
# Only SESSION_SECRET is uncommented: the Deploy to Cloudflare button asks for every secret listed here, and the rest
# are optional (ARCH.md §16 #101). Set one later in the dashboard: the Worker → Settings → Variables and Secrets.
# Signs everyone's sign-in cookie: any long random value — `openssl rand -hex 32` makes one. Keep a copy: /setup asks
# for it once, to show it's you setting the library up. (The app refuses the old example value, which anyone can read.)
SESSION_SECRET=
# Discogs personal access token (free account) — enables vinyl barcode/name lookup.
# DISCOGS_TOKEN=
# BoardGameGeek application token — board game search needs one since BGG went registration-only.
# Register an app at https://boardgamegeek.com/applications, then paste its token here.
# BGG_TOKEN=
# Optional: raises Google Books quota; books work keyless without it.
# GOOGLE_BOOKS_KEY=
# Optional front door: logged-out "/" redirects to /share/<token> instead of /login.
# Use the token of a published share; update after rotating that share.
# HOME_SHARE_TOKEN=
# Optional: this instance's identity for connections between Nalanda instances.
# Generate with `npm run federation:keygen`. Unset = connections disabled entirely.
# FEDERATION_PRIVATE_KEY='{"kty":"OKP","crv":"Ed25519","x":"…","d":"…"}'
# A restored copy of a production database (runbooks/backup-and-restore.md): set before the first
# page load, and this instance contacts none of the households its connections table names — no
# pull, no push, no live read. A plain variable, not a secret; production never sets it (ARCH.md §16 #92).
# FEDERATION_OFFLINE=1
